{"url": "https://www.monash.edu/graduate-research/future-students/apply", "final_url": "https://www.monash.edu/graduate-research/study/apply", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-10-30", "text": "Skip to content\nSkip to navigation\nHome\nMonash Australia\nMonash Australia\nMonash India\nMonash Indonesia\nMonash Malaysia\nMonash Prato\nMonash Suzhou\nMonash Boston Hub\nMonash Australia\nCourses\nMonash Online\nLibrary\nDonate\nSTAFF\nStaff\nStaff portal\nIntranet\nM-Space\nThe Insider\nSTAFF\nSTUDENTS\nStudents\nStudent portal\nStudent website\nMonash Connect\nMonash Online hub\nSTUDENTS\nALUMNI\nAlumni\nAlumni portal\nAlumni website\nALUMNI\nSEARCH\nGRADUATE RESEARCH\nHOME\nSTUDY\nSUPPORT AND RESOURCES\nSUPERVISION\nMORE\nAPPLY TO STUDY\nApplying with us\nHOW TO APPLY\nMonash offers Doctoral (PhD) and Master\u2019s by research degrees across all faculties, with campuses in Australia, Malaysia and Indonesia. This page guides new applicants through the steps to apply.\nBefore you begin, review the Application Submission Guide for a full list of required supporting documentation.\n1. Check your eligibility\nThe first step in your application is confirming you meet the eligibility requirements for a graduate research degree at Monash. There are three requirements to check:\nEnglish language proficiency\nAcademic entry requirements\nRelevant research or professional experience\nYou should also check your specific course, as some have additional entry requirements.\nExpand each section below to find out more.\nEnglish language proficiency\nAcademic entry requirements\nResearch or professional experience\nDon\u2019t yet meet the academic entry requirements?\nThere may still be a pathway into graduate research at Monash. We offer pathways through coursework degrees for applicants who have not yet completed a research-intensive qualification, and we recognise substantial professional or industry experience where it is relevant to your proposed research.\nExplore graduate research entry pathways\nApplying for a scholarship?\nCentrally managed scholarships for Australian campuses are awarded through a highly competitive process. The Graduate Research Committee prioritises applicants in accordance with the Research Training Program scholarship procedure.\nWhile applicants must meet the minimum academic and ELP requirements to be considered, this should not be interpreted as a guarantee of admission or scholarship support. In a high-demand and highly competitive environment, the number of well-qualified applicants consistently exceeds available places, requiring selection from among the strongest candidates.\nTo be considered for a scholarship, you must apply within an open scholarship round. See key dates below.\nFind out more about applying for scholarships, fees and funding opportunities.\n2. Before you apply\nA well-prepared application starts before you open the form. Work through the steps below to get ready.\nEach faculty has specific guidance on what they need from you. Select yours below to find out what\u2019s expected before you apply.\nArt, Design and Architecture \u2502 Arts \u2502 Business and Economics \u2502 Education \u2502 Engineering \u2502 Information Technology \u2502 Law \u2502 Medicine, Nursing and Health Sciences \u2502 Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences \u2502 Science\nFind a supervisor\nPrepare your research proposal\nGather your documents\n3. Key dates\nThe round you apply in determines when you would commence. Check the dates below and confirm your preferred faculty and course before you apply.\nFaculty preferred commencement dates\nSCHOLARSHIPS ROUNDS FOR:\nINTERNATIONAL APPLICANTS\nDOMESTIC APPLICANTS\nRound Application round dates Enrolment period\nR1 1 September \u2013 28 February* July \u2013 December (current year)\nR3 4 May \u2013 31 August January \u2013 June (following year)\n*Please note: R1 Closing date for 2027 has been brought forward from 31 March to 28 February.\nIMPORTANT: You can only submit one application per scholarship round or admission period (i.e. January - June or July - December). Ensure you confirm your preferred faculty, course and supervisor before you apply.\nAdmission only\nApplications for admission can be submitted at any time throughout the year.\nUse this application pathway if you are an applicant who:\nIs embedded in industry and are applying for an Industry PhD;\nHas secured, or is in the process of applying for external (i.e. not Monash) scholarship funding (industry, government, competitive award, or research grant; or\nAre a domestic Australian applicant applying for part-time admission; or\nAre applying for admission to our Malaysia or Indonesia campuses.\nWant to study at our Malaysia or Indonesia campuses?\nThe scholarship round dates published on this page apply to Australian campuses only. For information on applications, scholarship opportunities and closing dates at our international campuses, see:\nGraduate research at Monash University Malaysia\nGraduate research at Monash Indonesia\n4. Submit your application\nApplications are submitted through the online application portal. Before you begin, review the Application Submission Guide for a full list of required supporting documentation.\nApply now\n5. What happens next?\nOnce you submit your application it will be directed to your preferred supervisor and faculty for review. From there, processes vary based on faculty or campus - you may be contacted for an interview or further information, or you may receive an outcome directly.\nScholarship outcomes (Australia campuses): Applicants are normally notified of scholarship outcomes within six to ten weeks of the relevant application round closing. Admission offers are issued shortly afterwards.\nNote: for scholarship round 3 (international) in 2026, outcomes will be released in the week commencing 11th October 2026.\nAdmission outcomes (Australia Campuses)\nAdmission with Scholarship: Course offers are issued shortly after scholarship offers\nAdmission only: Masters by Research applicants, full-time PhD applicants with external funding, and PhD applicants who wish to enrol part-time, are typically processed within six weeks\nAdmission outcomes (Malaysia and Indonesia Campuses\nAdmission: applications are typically processed within six weeks\nScholarship: Refer to the Malaysia Scholarship information (outcomes are usually provided within 6 weeks of the closing of each scholarship round) and the Indonesia Scholarship information.\nOther application pathways\nLooking to apply for a joint award with Monash as the host institution, seek readmission, or transfer between graduate research courses? See other graduate research degrees.\nExplore other study pages\nScholarships\nWe offer a range of generous stipend and tuition fee scholarships to support you and your graduate research, so you can focus on what's important.\nHow to respond\nExplore how to respond to your offer online, submit changes of commencement date, and understand additional requirements.\nHow to enrol\nWelcome to Monash University! Take the next steps to secure your spot at Monash.\nThe Monash PhD\nDiscover a PhD that prepares you for success.\nJoint research awards\nDiscover how you can undertake one program of study while utilising the resources of two universities.\nOther research degrees\nThese include: Master of philosophy, Master's by research, professional doctorates, and higher doctorates.\nScholarships\nWe offer a range of generous stipend and tuition fee scholarships to support you and your graduate research, so you can focus on what's important.\nHow to respond\nExplore how to respond to your offer online, submit changes of commencement date, and understand additional requirements.\nHow to enrol\nWelcome to Monash University! Take the next steps to secure your spot at Monash.\nThe Monash PhD\nDiscover a PhD that prepares you for success.\nJoint research awards\nDiscover how you can undertake one program of study while utilising the resources of two universities.\nOther research degrees\nThese include: Master of philosophy, Master's by research, professional doctorates, and higher doctorates.\nReturn to study\nWe acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians\nCOMMUNITY\nFaculties\nLocations\nDiversity and inclusion\nSafety and security\nSustainability\nRESOURCES\nImportant dates\nHow to apply\nA-Z index\nPolicy Bank\nFAQs\nCONTACT\nContact us\nCampus maps\nJobs at Monash\nRecruit a student\nPay online\nNEWS\nLatest news\nMonash Lens\nPodcasts\nA Different Lens\nMonash Life\nON OUR SITE\nContact Us\nStaff intranet\nCourses and study options\nHow to apply\nSite map\nREGISTERED AUSTRALIAN UNIVERSITY\nABN: 12 377 614 012\nTEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140\nCRICOS PROVIDER NUMBER\nMonash University: 00008C\nMonash College: 01857J\nAUTHORISED BY\nExecutive Director, Marketing\nWebsite feedback\nLast updated: Oct 2026\nAccessibility\nDisclaimer & copyright\nTerms & conditions\nData privacy & cyber security\nData Consent Settings\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 Monash University\nWe use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which ones we use, and opt-out at any time. You can find more information in our Website Terms and Conditions\nAccept all\nCookie settings", "links": [["Home", "https://www.monash.edu/graduate-research"], ["Courses", "https://www.monash.edu/study/courses"], ["Monash Online", "https://online.monash.edu/"], ["Library", "https://www.monash.edu/library"], ["Donate", "https://www.monash.edu/giving"], ["Graduate Research", "https://www.monash.edu/graduate-research"], ["Home", "https://www.monash.edu/graduate-research/migr"], ["Study", "https://www.monash.edu/graduate-research/study"], ["Study", "https://www.monash.edu/graduate-research/study"], ["Why Monash", "https://www.monash.edu/graduate-research/study/why-monash"], ["How to apply", "htt